  type: 0
  title: '[L1]Basic Data Movement'
  content: "Lesson 1: Basic Data Movement\n Objective: Understand how to transfer
    data between registers, memory, and the stack.\n Instructions Covered:\n\n MOV:
    Moves data between registers or between memory and registers.\n MOV AX, BX ;
    AX gets the value in BX\n MOV AL, 5 ; AL gets the value 5\n\n PUSH and POP: Push
    data onto the stack and pop it back.\n PUSH AX ; Saves AX on the stack\n POP
    AX ; Retrieves the last value pushed into AX\n\n Exercise Application: You'll
    use MOV to set values in registers and PUSH/POP for managing values on the stack
    in Exercise 3 (Stack Spider)."
